#. translators: 1: service host name, 2: privacy policy URL.
#: disable-comments.php:322
#, php-format
msgid "If you agree, the plugin sends this to WPInsight (%1$s), WPDeveloper's usage-analytics service: your site URL and site name, WordPress version, site language and charset, PHP version, server software, whether it is a multisite, text direction, the server path of the plugin, your active and inactive plugins, your active theme and its version, the Disable Comments version, and your user account's email address so we can send you the discount coupon. It is sent once when you agree, then about once a day (only what changed). A daily report can also include the current logged-in user account email; a background report without a logged-in user omits email. Reports also include the plugin name and identifier, tracker version, activation status and marketing flag, service-assigned site identifier, and original site URL when available. When you deactivate the plugin, these details are sent again with your email address, deactivation time, and the reason and note you enter. Like any web request, it also reveals your server's IP address. No other service is contacted. This data lets us make sure this plugin always stays compatible with the most popular plugins and themes. No spam, I promise. <a href=\"%2$s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Privacy Policy</a>"
msgstr ""

